(A thing's list field passed to a value parameter is copied into it, as a
 named list is: what the function then does to the field, by its own name,
 is never seen through the parameter.)
A thing called note has
  a list called items.

a note called memo.
append "a" to memo's items.

To 'look after freeing' with a value called kept.
    Free memo's items.
    Print "kept after a free: {kept}".

To 'look after growing' with a value called kept.
    For each step from 1 to 40, append step to memo's items.
    Print "kept after growth: {kept}".

'look after growing' of memo's items.
Print "memo grew to {memo's items's length}".
'look after freeing' of memo's items.
Print "memo after the free: {memo's items}".
